cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use package-doctor in research, please cite it as below."
title: "package-doctor"
abstract: >-
  Finds the Python dependencies that sit at a trust boundary and have no one
  left to fix them. A two-axis model: escalation requires both curated
  trust-boundary exposure and evidence of lost remediation capacity, with
  advisories read under OSV's range semantics and ranked by CISA KEV and
  FIRST EPSS.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jayaweera
    given-names: Binuka
version: 0.8.4
date-released: "2026-09-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/binuka200/package-doctor"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/package-doctor/"
keywords:
  - dependencies
  - software supply chain
  - vulnerability management
  - open source maintenance
  - Python
